			"color":"#232",
			"widgets_values":[
				"Editorial cinematic technology product commercial. Use <Picture 1> as the exact opening frame.\n\nPreserve the exact appearance and structure of the transparent gaming mouse from the input image: the same transparent acrylic shell, scroll wheel, side buttons, internal circuit board, blue outer lighting, warm orange internal lighting, camera angle and black studio background. The mouse remains a single rigid manufactured product throughout the video. No deformation, no duplicated components, no extra buttons, no changing proportions, no text, no logo, no hands.\n\n[0.0s–1.5s]\nBegin exactly from <Picture 1>. The transparent mouse rests on a barely visible glossy black reflective surface. The electric-blue rim light and warm amber internal light slowly pulse brighter. The camera performs a smooth, deliberate push-in with subtle parallax, revealing the intricate circuitry beneath the transparent shell. Tiny floating dust particles appear in the dark background. Premium cinematic product photography, crisp acrylic refraction and realistic metallic reflections.\n\n[1.5s–3.2s]\nA fast, seamless cinematic transition into an extreme macro close-up of the ridged scroll wheel and the layered internal electronic components. The camera glides slowly along the side of the mouse. A narrow warm-orange scanning beam travels from the front toward the rear, illuminating the metallic components one by one. Thin electric-blue energy traces briefly flow through the circuit paths beneath the shell. The physical structure of the mouse remains completely intact and realistic.\n\n[3.2s–5.0s]\nThe camera rapidly pulls back into a dramatic low-angle hero shot. The mouse levitates only a few centimeters above the dark reflective surface and rotates slowly by approximately twenty degrees, stable and weightless. A circular blue-and-orange energy ring expands behind the mouse, sending a soft wave through the surrounding particles, then collapses inward and is absorbed into the mouse. The transparent edges produce a sharp blue rim-light flare. End on a clean, centered product silhouette, followed by a quick fade to pure black.\n\nAudio:\nDeep futuristic sub-bass pulses from the beginning. A subtle electronic room hum and delicate internal electrical crackling. One precise mechanical mouse click at 1.5 seconds. A glassy stereo whoosh during the macro transition. A rising electric charging sound begins at 3.2 seconds, followed by a clean cinematic impact at 4.6 seconds, then near silence during the final fade."
